# Portal type scale (admin ↔ agent)

Admin portal and agent/retailer portal must stay **visually matched** for base type size and sidebar density.

## Shared baseline (do not drift)

Both portals’ `app/globals.css`:

- `html { font-size: 106.25%; }` (~17px)
- Standard Tailwind tokens only:
  - `--text-xs: 0.75rem`
  - `--text-sm: 0.875rem`
  - `--text-base: 1rem`
  - `--text-lg: 1.125rem`
  - `--text-xl: 1.25rem`
  - `--text-2xl: 1.5rem`
  - `--text-3xl: 1.875rem`

Do **not** bump only admin (or only agent) root `%` or override `--text-*` larger/smaller without updating the other portal the same way.

## Sidebar / shell labels

Match retailer `AppShell` density:

- Top-level nav labels: `text-sm font-medium`
- Submenu / nested links: `text-sm`
- Section labels: ~`text-[11px]` uppercase tracking
- User card name / meta: ~`text-[14px]` / `text-[11px]`

Do not use oversized sidebar text (`text-base` / `text-[15px]+` on every nav row) in one portal only.

## When changing size

1. Edit **both** `apps/admin-portal/app/globals.css` and `apps/agent-portal/app/globals.css` together, **or**
2. Change a shared pattern in both shells (`AdminShell` ↔ agent `AppShell`).

One-off page micro-copy may use `text-[11px]` / `text-xs` where needed — do not “fix readability” by raising global root on a single portal.

## Daily 2FA card (agent portal)

Shared component is the **source of truth**: `apps/agent-portal/components/aeps/DailyVerifyCard.tsx` (Aadhaar-style ID card, verify-with tiles, RD device row, consent card, green→blue Scan fingerprint CTA, steps + tips strip). Used by `/aeps` (AePS + Aadhaar Pay) and `/dmt`.

DMT / Nepal / any new service 2FA gate must **render `DailyVerifyCard`** (only `service` / `continueLabel` differ). Do not hand-roll a gate card.
